WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:03.250
Their second win.

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.910
Eiga High is the first to get
a glimpse of the finish line.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.610
Odachi can't afford another loss.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.740
It seems the bouts are being hotly contested.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.060
Oh, you came,

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.640
Yamatokuni.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.450
It's been a long time.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.930
Shunkai-san. Master Shibakiyama.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.800
So is the Heisei era's greatest yokozuna
here to watch his son's victory?

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.460
That's partly why, yes, but...

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.260
I wanted to see them with my own eyes...

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.960
The young men who are
the future of sumo wrestling.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.170
<i>Fourth bout.</i>

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>On the east side, Ozeki-kun.</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.510
Okay.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.900
<i>On the west side, Daniel-kun.</i>

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.500
Here I go.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.860
Oh, it's the blond sumo wrestler!

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.520
You can do it, Daniel!

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.690
He's got such a cute smile!

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.480
What's going on? The crowd's gone wild.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.740
I believe it is partly due to there being
 so few Caucasians in school sumo,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.200
but his performances in the
tournament is a major factor, too.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.160
He may not have won
the individual tournament,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.920
but I hear he gave a good account
of himself against Kuze-san.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.130
For real?

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.240
His physique is flawless.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.720
Even the pros are watching
the progress of this foreigner.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.860
He's in the same boat as Bat.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:22.260
Foreigners can't attain
national treasure monikers,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.020
but he's pretty much on the same level.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.920
Our secret weapon from Europe.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.110
I've nicknamed him...

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.150
the Holy Sword, Excalibur!

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.570
Only you call him that.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.710
<i>As good as a national treasure...</i>

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.990
<i>He may be more than Ozeki can handle.</i>

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.020
Captain, stay level-headed.
You're good at that.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.960
It's strange...

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.090
Ushio-kun always stands squarely behind

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.710
his teammate in the ring
during team tournament bouts.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.720
How should I put it?

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.560
I guess I mean... it seems a kind thing to do.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.480
When they're next to one another, 
you can see how much taller he is!

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.480
Now isn't the time to compare physiques.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.450
Sumo is about spirit.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.070
You said that before the match.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.190
I think so, too.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.970
Your team is small, but very strong.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.210
I'm big, but I used to be very weak.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.330
I came to Japan because I liked sumo.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.870
I used to be weak, too.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.290
I didn't win a single bout until last year.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.090
Wow, that's seriously weak.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.860
Yeah, but...

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.510
I'm stronger now.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.820
So am I.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.520
In that sense, we are similar.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:48.890
Maybe so.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:53.820
<i>He's so passionate about sumo, he moved
to a different continent just to do it.</i>

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.150
<i>I've heard sumo's getting
more popular overseas,</i>

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:02.530
<i>but it still takes a lot of courage
to decide to take it up.</i>

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.790
<i>I think you love sumo the same way I do.</i>

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:16.460
<i>And you got stronger for the exact
same reason I did, I'm sure of it!</i>

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.730
Spirit!

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.270
Spirit!

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:58.610
Slap strikes.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:02.030
<i>He's unrelenting!</i>

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:07.070
<b>Bout 23
"Spirit"</b>

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.780
"Stronger now," huh?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.030
<i>It's true. Daniel used to be weak.</i>

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.890
<i>We had high hopes for
the exchange student,</i>

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:16.170
<i>but when we saw him in action,
he was just some beefed-up sumo fanatic.</i>

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.340
<i>For sure, he had a huge frame,</i>

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.750
<i>but he didn't have a clue how to use it.</i>

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:27.590
That Left-Arm Clamp looks
almost exactly like yours.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.140
<i>Everyone doing sumo wrestling right now</i>

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.440
<i>learned about the sport
from watching Yamatokuni.</i>

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.620
<i>Wanting to be like him</i>

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:47.220
<i>was reason enough to go to
a sumo club in the next town over.</i>

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:50.120
<i>Was it the same for you?</i>

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:54.200
<i>Were you there on another continent,
trying to copy Yamatokuni?</i>

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.830
<i>You're doing Yamatokuni's signature move:
the Left-Arm Clamp.</i>

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.460
<i>But I won't let you!</i>

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.540
<i>I won't let you seal my left arm!</i>

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.280
I'm sure it's less that he's copying my move

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.760
and more that he got it from Sosuke.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.520
Hang in there, captain!

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.900
Grind it out until you can grab him!

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.180
<i>Grind it out... In a battle of patience...</i>

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.770
<i>I can beat anyone!</i>

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.780
<i>What mental strength!</i>

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:26.660
<i>I have no doubt that your spirit
is every bit as strong as Onimaru's!</i>

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.830
<i>Ushio opened my eyes</i>

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.490
<i>to the thing that makes
sumo truly enjoyable!</i>

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.230
Captain.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:37.800
Go win this.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.780
<i>Tasting the joys of victory</i>

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:44.460
<i>has made me love sumo all the more!</i>

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:48.720
<i>They might really be two peas in a pod.</i>

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.800
<i>They were both weaklings up until recently.</i>

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:56.310
<i>But both of them met a person</i>

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.150
<i>who changed them completely.</i>

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.810
<i>They met their heroes.</i>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.890
Ozeki!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.230
Daniel!

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.670
<i>Grind it out.</i>

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:08.560
<i>Nice and steady.</i>

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.820
<i>If I can get my arm outside his,
I can overpower him!</i>

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.330
<i>I need to get my right arm on
the outside like he taught me!</i>

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.790
<b>Eiga
University
High
School
Sumo
Club</b>

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.790
<i>I crossed the seas
just to do what I love.</i>

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.830
<i>I thought I could become a pro sumo wrestler.</i>

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:25.290
<i>But I got a cold, hard dose of reality.</i>

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.500
<i>I can't beat anyone!</i>

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.110
<i>But why? I'm bigger than everyone here...</i>

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:34.010
<i>Sumo... isn't fun.</i>

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:39.140
<i>After spending my first year
thinking like that, I met </i>him<i>.</i>

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.790
<i>He was still in middle school</i>

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.400
<i>and was coming to Eiga High
the following year,</i>

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:49.560
<i>but the club members at the time at least
didn't seem very welcoming.</i>

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.890
They say he refuses to contest actual bouts.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.910
Huh? What's up with that?

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.030
Does he think he's better than us?

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.660
<i>I didn't know who he was.</i>

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:06.290
<i>But when I fought him,
I couldn't help blurting out...</i>

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:09.300
Y-Yamatokuni!

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.260
<i>Later on, they told me who he was,</i>

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.680
<i>and instead of being shocked,
it made total sense to me.</i>

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.640
You're incredible.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:23.600
I'm sure sumo's a lot of fun
when you're as strong as you are.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.860
So much fun that you don't care
what other people say.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.580
Hmm...

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:32.190
I do care about what other people say.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:39.450
I worry about whether my sumo
lives up to the Yamatokuni name.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:44.580
And worrying about that
shows that I'm weak.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:52.460
I need to focus my full attention on
the sumo ring and tune out what people say.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:57.390
To do otherwise would be rude to
my opponent and to sumo as a whole.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:01.640
Do you enjoy sumo?

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.250
Hmm...

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.150
I do like sumo.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:07.650
But as for whether I enjoy it...

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.470
I don't know.

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.650
I have nothing...

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.780
except sumo.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.200
I must devote myself to it.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.920
<i>I felt like he was telling me
how naïve I was being.</i>

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.210
<i>That was the mindset of a guy
trying to make sumo his livelihood.</i>

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:32.810
<i>Because I was so weak, I decided
to train harder than him.</i>

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.530
<i>If he did 300 stomps, I'd do 400!</i>

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.850
<i>If that wasn't enough...</i>

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.920
<i>I'd know it was time to give up!</i>

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:46.940
Daniel. Sosuke. Starting today,

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.110
you're training in the first-string ring.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:55.990
<i>And now, I enjoy sumo so much...</i>

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.950
<i>So very, very much!</i>

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.710
He couldn't grab him,
so he switched to strikes!

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.420
Even at a distance, he's a beast!

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:10.170
<i>Your rapid improvement proves that
sumo is all about spirit.</i>

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.670
<i>Yeah, Sosuke was on the third string
and being treated like an outcast.</i>

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:20.760
<i>Daniel was the only one
who kept challenging him.</i>

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.390
<i>Those who froze him out didn't get very far.</i>

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:28.810
<i>And those who saw being able to spar with
Sosuke every day as a golden opportunity</i>

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.560
<i>now turn out for Eiga's first string.</i>

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.700
<i>So you get struck harder 
than that every day?</i>

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.990
<i>Is that what you're telling me?</i>

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.030
Go, Ozeki!

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.910
This is like a sneak preview 
of Onimaru versus Kusanagi.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.660
That means he has to win.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.790
<i>Ushio wants to beat Kuze.</i>

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:57.170
<i>Which means I can't lose
to Kuze's style of sumo!</i>

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.340
Good, the captain's in position!

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.660
<i>Wait for him to move forward,
then go for the outside.</i>

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.350
<i>I can reach around him!</i>

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:09.130
<i>I'm weak, so I'm always in fear of losing.</i>

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:13.790
<i>Ozeki-san, have I struck
at least a little fear in you?</i>

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.240
<i>Are you having fun right now?!</i>

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.200
<i>Right overarm throw!</i>

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.820
<i>Great Serpent Cleaver!</i>

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:25.950
<b>Great</b>

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:26.450
<b>Cleaver</b>

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.370
<b>Great</b>

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:26.450
<b>Serpent</b>

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:26.700
<b>Cleaver</b>

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.370
<b>Serpent</b>

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:27.370
<b>Cleaver</b>

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:33.920
<i>Daniel, you said we're similar,
but you're wrong.</i>

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.130
<i>Your goal seems to be imitating Kuze,</i>

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.240
<i>but me and Ushio are nothing like that!</i>

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.220
<i>It was only once out of the hundreds 
or thousands of times we sparred,</i>

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:49.850
<i>but I actually beat Ushio.</i>

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.850
<i>I was so happy, I treated myself to cake.</i>

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.750
<i>The next day, Ushio was still pouting.</i>

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.530
<i>And that made me happy, too.</i>

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:06.080
<i>Because me and Ushio... are rivals!</i>

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:09.760
Captain!

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:10.590
You did it!

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:11.750
Yes!

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.370
Captain!

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.500
On the east side,
with a beltless arm throw...

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.750
Ozeki-kun wins!

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.400
He's got what it takes to be a national 
treasure, but he still needs work.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.970
No, I should take nothing away from Ozeki
and the patience that won him the bout.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.020
<i>It's 2-2 now.</i>

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.970
<i>I've done all I can do.</i>

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.520
<i>Now...</i>

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:42.470
<i>It's time for you to win, Ushio!</i>

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.460
<i>Team tournament final, fifth bout.</i>

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.600
<i>On the east side, Ushio-kun.</i>

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.350
<i>On the west side, Kuze-kun.</i>

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:55.040
Onimaru Kunitsuna and the Kusanagi Sword.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:59.550
Two national treasures will slug it out
to decide the winner of the team tournament.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.430
That's not all that's at stake.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.250
This bout may well be their ticket

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:07.390
to joining the pro league via entry into
the All-Japan National Championships.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:09.620
Listen to that crowd.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.890
Everyone already acknowledges his ability.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.780
Even if he doesn't make it this year,

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:18.480
it's only a matter of time before he goes pro.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.180
You've got it all wrong.

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:24.320
He doesn't just want to be a pro.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.770
He wants to be a yokozuna.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:30.210
<i>He doesn't have an unlimited
number of chances.</i>

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:34.200
<i>How does he expect to become
a yokozuna if he doesn't win today?</i>

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:35.800
Guys...

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.960
Did you enjoy doing sumo?

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:41.810
Yuma.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:48.050
Your steady, earnest efforts
kept the sumo club going.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:50.110
Chihiro.

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:55.040
Your experience as a champion
instilled confidence in the team.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.140
Kirihito.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:00.430
You put us on the right path.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.050
Kei.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:06.450
We can't forget you.
Your courage inspired us all.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.100
Hori-chan. Reina.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:13.250
We've all seen the incredible 
job you do in supporting us.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:14.840
Captain.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.580
You protected the sumo club for three years,

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.390
and united team members
with strong personalities.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.380
Thank you for supporting us.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:27.830
I'm glad you all joined the sumo club
and got enjoyment out of sumo.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.130
Thank you.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.450
Idiot.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:35.140
We're the one who are grateful.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:38.890
Thanks to you, we all learned to love sumo.

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:43.610
This is our last sumo bout as a team.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.820
Don't leave with any regrets.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.400
Go win this, Ushio!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:50.860
Yeah!

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:53.120
You won't win.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:59.250
The sumo gods have taken up
residence inside him.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.750
Sosuke!

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:07.580
<i>This feeling again... I rather like it.</i>

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:11.760
<i>This silence engulfs us, as if we are
the only two people in the world.</i>

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:16.010
<i>I can forget everything else
and just do sumo.</i>

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:17.320
Hey.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.140
You don't want to hear it?

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:22.230
You don't want to hear these cheers?

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:29.190
I came here so I could 
hear this sound again.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:30.950
<i>Louder...</i>

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.450
<i>Even louder...</i>

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.710
<i>Loud enough to reach the heavens!</i>

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:47.060
<i>I see. That's how you do things.</i>

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.930
I've been waiting for this for a long time.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:52.340
Yeah. So have I.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.640
We started our bout that day...

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:57.840
...and today is the day we end it.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:04.190
Now, let's put everything on the line.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:12.070
<i>He was smiling until
he stepped into the sumo ring.</i>

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.820
<i>Their bout of destiny.</i>

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:19.580
<i>At last.</i>

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:22.540
Spirit!

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:24.420
<i>A spider stance.</i>

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.040
<i>Flickering</i>

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:27.750
<i>like fire.</i>

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:32.400
<i>I've waited so long for this!</i>

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:33.600
Yes!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:34.490
After the charge...

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:35.640
...Onimaru's on top!

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.140
Go!

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:41.810
<i>The do-or-die bouts I've survived,</i>

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:43.560
<i>the strong opponents I've devoured,</i>

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.360
<i>and the confidence I've rebuilt...</i>

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.490
<i>kindle my fire ever more!</i>

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:54.200
<i>He's loading up and attacking head-on!</i>

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.830
<i>I'm not just rushing in head-on!</i>

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.330
<i>I'm choosing my target</i>

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.330
<i>and focusing on it!</i>

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:05.420
<i>That's the rising strike Tennoji used.</i>

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.040
It's working!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:10.860
Kuze is quick on his feet!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.010
Don't let him get away!

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:17.220
<i>I know an even faster sumo wrestler!</i>

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.730
<i>Don't underestimate him just
because he has a short reach.</i>

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:27.480
<i>Once he gets in close,
Hinomaru's strikes are a powerful weapon.</i>

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.980
<i>Having shorter arms
means he can strike faster.</i>

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:34.110
<i>He even held his own against Odenta,
the most powerful striker in high school sumo.</i>

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:39.740
<i>If he catches you when you're off-balance,
each strike he delivers</i>

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:42.120
<i>hits harder than it looks.</i>

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:43.620
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:46.420
Kusanagi's been forced back
to the edge of the ring?!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.920
<i>I could never have gotten this far on my own.</i>

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.930
Go!

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:54.340
<i>But my team was there for me!</i>

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.280
Push!

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.430
<i>We've taken everything
fate could throw at us,</i>

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:00.470
<i>and overcome it all to get here,</i>

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.060
<i>Kuze Sosuke!</i>

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.260
<i>In just a short amount of time,</i>

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:12.980
<i>you have truly become strong.</i>

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.240
<i>But so have I.</i>

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:19.370
<i>I will beat you and join the pro league.</i>

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.550
<i>Kuze's every movement 
is eroding my stamina...</i>

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:26.770
<i>and my spirit.</i>

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.330
<i>If I make the wrong move even once...</i>

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.090
<i>I'm dead.</i>

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:34.800
Hinomaru!

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.470
<i>Kuze never rushes or takes risks.</i>

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:41.730
<i>There are no holes in his offense!</i>

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:43.360
Don't stop!

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:45.390
Move off to the side to get him moving!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.650
<i>This rush... Is it excitement?</i>

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:52.150
<i>Or is it fear?</i>

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:57.860
Sosuke, what is a yokozuna?

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.200
<b>Yamatokuni
Stable</b>

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.200
One mistake in sumo

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:03.910
can turn out to be fatal.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:08.080
But to err is human. We all make mistakes.

